# Styling log

Before any UI, layout, token, or HeroUI component work, read [STYLING.md](STYLING.md).

After any visual change in the same turn, update `STYLING.md`:

- Tokens (color, type, space, radius, motion)
- Primitives (links, buttons, type scale, lists)
- Components (header, work row, case-study layout, etc.)
- Changelog, newest first: date, what changed, why

If it is not in `STYLING.md`, it did not happen.

Do not invent a parallel design system. Override HeroUI via CSS variables and documented classes only.
